      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Roanoke Canal Museum and Trail is one of the city's oldest historical sites.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roanoke_Rapids%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The construction of the Roanoke Rapids Dam in the early 20th century created Gaston Lake and hydroelectric power.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/roanoke-rapids-30114",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Roanoke Rapids once planned Carolina Crossroads, an entertainment district founded by local business developers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roanoke_Rapids%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Businessmen like Sam Patterson used the Roanoke River's rapids to power textile mills, sparking the town's growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roanoke_Rapids%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Roanoke Rapids is located at the eastern edge of the North Carolina Piedmont, on the Roanoke River at the fall line.",
